    "node-196v4e3": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim that 'Maintenance acceptance signature was not yet signed at notification time' is supported by the work package cover (IA-S02) which states 'Maintenance acceptance signature: not yet signed at notification time.' However, the node's detail asserts this means 'Work-boundary release pending; maintenance receiver M-A had not accepted the boundary when air loss occurred.' The evidence supports the lack of a signature but does not independently establish that no physical boundary acceptance (e.g., verbal confirmation or other procedural step) occurred. A blank field is not proof of absence of action.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Evidence showing whether M-A verbally confirmed, physically verified, or otherwise accepted the maintenance boundary prior to 10:00 AM despite the unsigned signature.","question":"Did Maintenance receiver M-A perform any physical verification or verbal acceptance of the work boundary before the air loss at approximately 10:00 AM?"
    },
    "node-hddaa6": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim that 'Temporary instruction attachment field was blank at issue time' is supported by IA-S02. However, the node's detail asserts this means 'No temporary instruction attached... ECP-1SC-04 revision 3 issued but no approved temp instruction for this specific boundary change or routing update.' The evidence confirms a blank field and an existing ECP; it does not prove that *no* other valid temporary instruction existed (e.g., one held separately, verbally authorized, or attached to another document). A missing attachment in the folder is not proof of absence of a safeguard.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Evidence showing whether any alternative temporary instruction was issued, approved, and communicated for this specific boundary change/routing update at issue time.","question":"Was an alternative temporary instruction (not on IA-S02) issued or verbally authorized to cover the boundary change or routing update?"
    },
